  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "f(x) = \\begin{cases} 1/q & \\text{if } x = p/q \\text{ in lowest terms} \\\\ 0 & \\text{if } x \\in \\mathbb{R} \\setminus \\mathbb{Q} \\end{cases}",
    "plain": "Thomae's function is famously continuous at every irrational and discontinuous at every rational. Lebesgue's criterion says: Riemann integrability is equivalent to continuity almost everywhere. Since rationals form a measure-zero set, Thomae's function is Riemann integrable. This problem formalizes this argument in Lean 4 using Mathlib's measure theory.",
